---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const updated = '10 November 2026';
---

<Base
  title="Terms of Use"
  description="Terms of use for WattFlow's no tax on tips and overtime calculators, including the estimate-only disclaimer and the absence of any warranty."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="page prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">Terms</p>
      <h1>Terms of use</h1>
      <p class="small muted">Last updated {updated}.</p>

      <div class="note note--warn">
        <strong>Read this part.</strong> The calculators give estimates of federal income tax only, based on IRS forms and
        guidance as of the date shown on each page. They are not tax advice and do not replace your own return, your W-2
        or 1099, the official IRS instructions, or a tax professional.
      </div>

      <h2>1. What this service is</h2>
      <p>
        This site provides free, browser-based calculators and guides about the no tax on tips and no tax on overtime
        deductions. The calculations run on your device; we do not receive the figures you enter.
      </p>

      <h2>2. No warranty</h2>
      <p>
        The service is provided “as is” and “as available”, without warranty of any kind, express or implied, including
        fitness for a particular purpose, accuracy or non-infringement. Tax rules and IRS forms change, and draft forms
        can differ from the final versions.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Your responsibility to verify</h2>
      <p>
        You are responsible for checking any result before relying on it — against your own tax documents, the current
        IRS forms and instructions, or with a qualified professional.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Not financial, legal, tax or accounting advice</h2>
      <p>Nothing on this site is financial, legal, tax or accounting advice.</p>

      <h2>5. Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>You agree not to use this service:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>to attempt to disrupt, overload or reverse-engineer the site;</li>
        <li>to scrape or republish its content as your own; or</li>
        <li>in any way that breaks applicable law.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>6. Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the maximum extent permitted by law, we are not liable for any indirect, incidental, special, consequential or
        punitive damages, or for any loss — including tax, interest or penalties — arising from your use of the service
        or from a decision made on the basis of a calculator result. Where liability cannot be excluded, it is limited to
        the greater of the amount you paid us (which, for the free calculators, is zero) or the minimum permitted by law.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Third-party names and links</h2>
      <p>
        Company and product names, such as DoorDash or Uber, are the trademarks of their owners and appear only to
        describe who may be affected by a rule. This site is not affiliated with, endorsed by or sponsored by them or by
        the IRS. Links to third-party sites are provided for convenience; we are not responsible for their content.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Intellectual property</h2>
      <p>The site’s own text, design and code are ours.</p>

      <h2>9. Availability and changes</h2>
      <p>
        We may change, suspend or discontinue any part of the service at any time, and may update these terms; the date at
        the top of this page will change when we do.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions about these terms: <a href="/contact/">contact us</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
